  "published": "2026-11-07T10:18:16.72Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.11.0 is the first nuget.org release since 1.8.7. Rebuild your app after upgrading.\n\nBreaking changes since 1.8.7:\n- Build your product's public key into the app (1.10): LicenseClientOptions.PublicKey (Dashboard > Product > Settings > RSA keys > Build into your app), AdditionalPublicKeys for a key rotation, or an embedded LicenPro.PublicKey.txt resource. A key in licenpro.settings.json or appsettings.json is ignored. Without a key, validation returns PublicKeyNotConfigured.\n- A changed license file, or one signed with another key, returns SignatureMismatch (was ValidationFailed).\n- LicenseClient.ConnectSessionAsync returns SessionConnectResult and DisconnectAsync returns bool: the source still compiles, but apps built against 1.8.x must be rebuilt.\n- Metered errors without an error code: a 403 maps to AccessDenied (was FeatureNotEntitled), a 409 to Conflict (was ConcurrencyConflict) and a 5xx to ServerError.\n\nNew since 1.8.7:\n- Device time protection (1.11): setting the clock back gains nothing for expiry, trial, grace or cache decisions. A trial extension or end set on the server reaches an offline device through a lease signed with your product key.\n- Offline check-in (1.11, off by default, set per product): an offline device must reach the server every N days; after the grace period, validation returns the new status CheckInRequired until it connects once.\n- One-click product updates with signed update packages, verified with your product key.\n- Metered retry safety (1.9): MeterManager.ConsumeWithRetryAsync and LicenseClient.ConsumeMeterWithRetryAsync re-send the same operation id, so a lost response is never charged twice.\n- LicenseClient implements IDisposable as well as IAsyncDisposable (VB.NET Using blocks).\n- The SDK's own cache file is now licenpro.cache; an old SDK cache named license.bin is moved once, and your own license file is never changed.\n\nLanguages: .NET and VB.NET use this package. Python and other languages use the same code through the LicenPro native library (lp_* functions; JSON unchanged apart from the new status values).",
